  "body": "In the HTML Spec, the Constraint Validation IDL is repeated numerous times in\r\n\r\n* select\r\n* input\r\n* textarea\r\n* object\r\n* fieldset\r\n* ElementInternals \r\n\r\nIt appears as though the properties can benefit from a `ConstraintValidationMixin` which helps us as users scripting Custom Elements stay on par with with spec and author expectations of custom elements that mimic native ones.\r\n\r\nAs it is now, it's unclear if these IDL attributes/properties are meant to be static, or if we need to check each and every control to find differences. I do see a small difference with `[setCustomValidity](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-cva-setcustomvalidity)` and `[setValidity](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-elementinternals-setvalidity)`, the former being native elements, and the latter being Custom Elements. But I would imagine those functions wouldn't be part of said mixin.",
